"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"The answer frames the checklist as suggested diligence, not a mandatory approval rule. It covers all three requested areas. Selection: criteria, compared alternatives and conflicts. Relevant-market expertise: experience with similar strategies and underlying assets, hedging and inventory sourcing, spreads, and coordination with authorized participants. Capital and seed support: who commits it, for how long, on what terms, and whether it is guaranteed or discretionary. It also distinguishes temporary LMM/affiliate market-making seed from durable investor assets. It does not assume seed is assured, since it asks what happens if support is withdrawn, and it probes asset retention after support ends, which implies subsidized investors can leave. Minor omission: calling investor assets 'durable' could suggest permanence, and it never says outright that investor assets are not necessarily permanent. The retention question largely covers this, so it is not a substantive error.\"}","ttft_ms":1876,"type":"result","duration_ms":4636,"uuid":"88615083-80f7-46b4-98b7-2ec04d0dd1c4","ttft_stream_ms":545,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":545,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
